  No one knows all the spoilers by heart, I don't think.

  Back to general advice:

  - Play carefully.  More carefully than you have been, judging 
    by the state of your armor.

  - A common pet on a leash can be very helpful in detecting 
    traps, if used properly.  (This is a little known and never
    used trick, as far as I know.)

  - Heck, the 's'earch command is rarely used for finding 
    completely unsuspected traps, as far as I can see.

  - Re-read the Guidebook!

  - READ ALL THE MESSAGES YOU GET.

  - Check every non-cursed piece of armor for enchantment.

  - There is a font of information guaranteed to be in every 
    game.  You've been past it at least once.  Note down 
    carefully what it tells you.  (i.e. learn to copy/paste).


  One poster here proved that you can get quite a distance into 
the game completely unspoiled.  (A pet disaster got him in the 
end - his attention seeking kitten jumped on the keyboard and 
managed to #quit him out of the game.)




